T2.5 / T2.6 reductions -- two target-specific questions
=======================================================

NOT a binCV-versus-OpenCV comparison. Both questions compare binCV against
binCV, so ARCHITECTURE 10.3's denominator does not apply to either; the OpenCV
table for these kernels is results/reduce_benchmark.log.

Q1  Does the SHIPPED bulk countNonZero beat the per-word popcount loop that D-6
    forbids the public API from making possible?
Q2  Does composing ARCHITECTURE 7.5's 2x2 covariance out of the T2.6 primitives
    (three calls, therefore three traversals) cost materially more than one
    fused traversal issuing the identical popcounts?

DECISION RULES FOR BOTH WERE WRITTEN BEFORE MEASURING and live in the source:
benchmark/reduce_target_benchmark.cpp. Summarised:
  Q1  bulk within +/-15% of the per-word loop -> D-6's INTERFACE decision stands,
      ARCHITECTURE 6.2's IMPLEMENTATION claim does not; fix the documents, record
      the numbers, change no kernel (vectorization is Phase 5).
  Q2  composition > 15% worse than fused -> widen T2.10's brief to measure a
      covariance-shaped entry point BEFORE T3.6 is written; do not add one now.

PLATFORM: the reference device -- AUTHORITATIVE for both questions, which are
about the primary target (EXPERIMENTS.md "Measurement platforms").

  device:           pi4
  cpu:              Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Rev 1.5 (Cortex-A72)
  arch / kernel:    aarch64 / 6.18.34+rpt-rpi-v8
  compiler:         g++ (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0, Release (-O2 -DNDEBUG)
  governor:         performance (restored to ondemand on exit)
  core pinning:     taskset -c 3
  throttled before / after: throttled=0x0 / throttled=0x0  (every run)

THREE RUNS, because one cannot show that a ratio reproduced.

  run   bulk ns/px  per-word ns/px  ratio   vector-accum ns/px  headroom
   1      0.04109      0.04094      1.00x        0.02333         1.76x
   2      0.03800      0.03773      0.99x        0.02045         1.86x
   3      0.03992      0.03970      0.99x        0.02209         1.81x

  run   composed ns/kp   fused ns/kp   composed/fused
   1        844.6           650.9          1.30x
   2        841.0           644.8          1.30x
   3        841.1           646.1          1.30x

READING Q1. The bulk entry point is worth NOTHING today against the loop shape it
exists to prevent: 0.99-1.00x. That is not a contradiction of D-6, it is a
statement about the implementation -- the emitted interior loop crosses the
GPR/NEON boundary once per word and accumulates in a general-purpose register,
which is precisely the per-word cost, so the two loops are the same loop. The
vector-accumulator row is a HEADROOM PROBE at the IDENTICAL 64-bit load width
(the only difference is that the running total stays in a NEON register and
crosses back once per row): 1.8x, available to Phase 5, not taken here. A wider
load would be a second variable and was deliberately not mixed in.

READING Q2. countAndSplit is single-pass as T2.6 requires. The COMPOSITION is
not: three calls visit each region word three times and load it three times, and
that is 1.30x, reproducibly -- with the popcount count identical between the two,
so the delta is redundant traversal rather than extra work per word. 1.30x
exceeds T2.10's own 15% threshold, so the composed-versus-fused axis is now part
of T2.10's brief; the interface was NOT changed on the strength of this
measurement, because choosing T2.6's shape before the experiment is the mistake
T2.6 exists to avoid.

Full output of run 3 follows.

